# Wave W17-Z (Route 216): bridge floor — the causeway’s paved run: pale blue-grey stone paving laid in regular joints, packed snow becoming stone bridge — the design’s stone bridge over the chasm drawn in the kind’s own art, art layer only, the shipped path cells never moving (design: the snow bridge road out of Mt. Apex’s north door, one stone span over the chasm). Split from every sand path in the fleet by material entire (paved stone vs sand) and from the Apex halls’ dressed flags behind it by exposure: those flags are roofed, this paving takes the weather.
